<% contrast = @manifest["contrast"] %>
<% genes = @manifest["genes"] %>
<% clustering = @manifest["clustering"] if @manifest["clustering"].is_a?(Hash) && @manifest["clustering"]["status"] == "completed" %>
<% baseline = clustering && clustering["silhouette_baseline"] %>
<% question = @manifest["time"].present? ? "It tested: #{@manifest["question"]}" : "It compared #{contrast["test_level"]} with #{contrast["reference_level"]} (the reference)." %>
MicroNet RNA-seq Results

Hello,

Your differential expression analysis (Job #<%= @job.job_number %>) is complete. <%= question %>

Summary
- Design: <%= @manifest["design"] %>
- Samples analyzed: <%= @manifest["samples"]["in_model"] %>
- Genes tested: <%= genes["tested"] %> of <%= genes["in_input"] %> in your count matrix
- Significant genes: <%= genes["significant"] %><% unless genes["significant_up"].nil? %> (<%= genes["significant_up"] %> higher and <%= genes["significant_down"] %> lower in <%= contrast["test_level"] %>)<% end %>
<% if clustering %>
- Gene clusters: <%= clustering["clusters"] %> (silhouette <%= format("%.2f", clustering["silhouette"]) %>)
<% end %>
<% if baseline %>
- Silhouette reliability check: actual <%= format("%.2f", baseline["actual"]) %>, shuffled baseline <%= format("%.2f", baseline["shuffled_mean"]) %>, difference <%= format("%+.2f", baseline["difference"]) %> (near 0 would mean no better than random patterns)
<% end %>

Attached
<% @file_names.each do |name| %>
- <%= name %>
<% end %>

README.txt explains every file, the settings used, and how the results were computed.
<% if @warnings.present? %>

Please Note
<% @warnings.each do |warning| %>
- <%= warning[:analysis] %>: <%= warning[:message] %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

For more information, check out the papers under the Resources page of MicroNet.

Thank you for using MicroNet!

Regards,
The MicroNet Team
